-- Hand-built, deliberately VALID instance of DerivedFK (regular USE SOIL
-- statements, not a Kodkod/SMT search). Two Widgets and two Gadgets,
-- every Gadget's targetname genuinely matching a distinct Widget's
-- wname, so WidgetNameMatches holds for both. No link is inserted into
-- FK_Gadget_Widget -- `widget' is a derived end, recomputed dynamically
-- by USE's own evaluator from the any()-match predicate, never a
-- materialized link a SOIL script could insert into.
--
-- NoMatchIsUndefined is EXPECTED to fail here (documented via
-- soilKnownOutOfScopeInvariants in manifest.json): it demands every
-- Gadget's derived widget be UNDEFINED, which is structurally impossible
-- whenever WidgetNameMatches also holds across a non-empty population --
-- the two invariants are near-complementary per Gadget, not independent
-- checks the way PriceCalc's own pair are.

!create widgetA : Widget
!set widgetA.wname := 'alpha'

!create widgetB : Widget
!set widgetB.wname := 'beta'

!create gadget1 : Gadget
!set gadget1.targetname := 'alpha'

!create gadget2 : Gadget
!set gadget2.targetname := 'beta'
